    "answer": {
      "short": "Tax liability of \\$2833.25.",
      "worked": "Using 52 weeks and 26 fortnights per year:\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Gross income} &= 30\\times35\\times52\\\\\n\\text{Gross income} &= \\$54\\,600\\\\\n\\text{Taxable income} &= 54\\,600-550\\\\\n\\text{Taxable income} &= \\$54\\,050\\\\\n\\text{Excess} &= 54\\,050-45\\,000\\\\\n\\text{Excess} &= \\$9050\\\\\n\\text{Tax payable} &= 5092+0.325\\times9050\\\\\n\\text{Tax payable} &= \\$8033.25\\\\\n\\text{Total instalments} &= 200\\times26\\\\\n\\text{Total instalments} &= \\$5200\\\\\n\\text{Refund/liability balance} &= 5200-8033.25\\\\\n\\text{Refund/liability balance} &= -\\$2833.25\n\\end{align*}$$\nShirley has paid too little tax, so she has a tax liability of \\$2833.25.",
